@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+Annotations: |
+  Gives every HTTP response a correlation id, reused across a chain of
+  internal calls: an `x-request-id` middleware that trusts a well-formed
+  incoming header or generates a fresh one, writes it to the response, and
+  publishes it through an AsyncLocalStorage-backed store so application code
+  handling the request (log statements, services, filters, ...) can read the
+  exact same id without touching the request or response objects. The
+  middleware is plain (req, res, next) code with no platform-specific
+  branches, so it runs identically whether the owning application is built
+  on the Express or the Fastify adapter — both support Express-style
+  middleware registration via `app.use()`.
+
+---
+
+"REQUEST_ID_HEADER()":
+  location: request-id.constants.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Name of the header (`x-request-id`) the middleware reads an incoming
+    correlation id from and writes the resolved id to on every response.
+
+"requestIdMiddleware(req: Object<string, any>, res: Object<string, any>, next: Object<string, any>)":
+  location: request-id.middleware.ts
+  annotations: |
+    (req, res, next) middleware, registered via `app.use()`, that resolves
+    the request's correlation id and sets it as a response header before
+    continuing the chain.
+
+    Algorithm:
+    1. Read the incoming `x-request-id` header; accept it only if it is a
+       single string matching the safe id pattern (bounded length, no
+       characters that could corrupt a response header), otherwise treat it
+       as absent
+    2. Generate a new id via `randomUUID()` when no usable incoming id was
+       found
+    3. Write the resolved id back as the `x-request-id` response header
+    4. Run the remainder of the request (the `next()` call and everything it
+       triggers, synchronously or asynchronously) inside
+       `RequestIdStorage.run`, so application code executing later in the
+       same request can retrieve the same id
+
+"RequestIdStorage()":
+  location: request-id.storage.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Thin wrapper around a module-level `AsyncLocalStorage<string>` that
+    propagates the current request's correlation id through async control
+    flow, independent of which platform adapter produced it.
+  methods:
+    "run(requestId: string, callback: Object<string, any>) -> result: any": |
+      Runs `callback` with `requestId` bound as the active store value for
+      its entire (possibly async) execution.
+    "get() -> requestId: string | undefined": |
+      Returns the correlation id bound by the innermost enclosing `run` call,
+      or undefined outside of one.
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 17/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents the request-id cell: the middleware that assigns and reflects a
+  correlation id on every HTTP response, and the AsyncLocalStorage-backed
+  store that exposes it to application code without adapter-specific access
+  or parsing the response back out. Kept adapter-agnostic so it behaves
+  identically for services built on the Express adapter and the Fastify
+  adapter alike.
